 Since $x+4609 \equiv 2104 \pmod{12}$, we can simplify the congruence by reducing 4609 and 2104 modulo 12. First, we find the remainders when 4609 and 2104 are divided by 12. \[
4609 \div 12 = 384 \text{ remainder } 1 \Rightarrow 4609 \equiv 1 \pmod{12}
\] \[
2104 \div 12 = 175 \text{ remainder } 4 \Rightarrow 2104 \equiv 4 \pmod{12}
\] Therefore, the congruence $x + 4609 \equiv 2104 \pmod{12}$ simplifies to \[ x + 1 \equiv 4 \pmod{12} \] Subtracting 1 from both sides gives \[ x \equiv 3 \pmod{12} \] The smallest positive integer $x$ that satisfies this congruence is 3. </think> <answer> $3$ </answer>

